# The archives under here are FIXTURES, not upstream tarballs, and they must
# reach a clone as their exact bytes.
#
# testing/fixtures/shell/tree/roll.tar.gz is two bytes and its twin under
# openwith/ is empty, and both are named .tar.gz for one reason: to prove the
# LONGEST matching suffix wins, so a .tar.gz does not open in a decompressor.
# The file chooser's golden frame prints the size, so any filter that stores
# something else in their place (a pointer, a normalised line ending) comes
# back as a failing layout test with nothing pointing at the cause. These
# lines unset every filter and text conversion for them, whatever a root
# .gitattributes says.
*.tar.gz  !filter !diff !merge -text
*.tar.xz  !filter !diff !merge -text
*.tar.bz2 !filter !diff !merge -text
*.tar.zst !filter !diff !merge -text
*.tgz     !filter !diff !merge -text
*.zip     !filter !diff !merge -text
